    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d706">

                <pb facs="0652" n="568" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg568"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 891.48/65</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of the American Committee for Armenian and
                        Syrian Relief</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Vickrey</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Department of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">New York</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-07-05">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 5, 1918</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received July 6.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gentlemen</hi>: Sometime ago Mirza Ali-Kuli Khan, Chargé d’Affaires of the
                    Persian Legation, asked me as secretary of the American Committee for Armenian
                    and Syrian Relief to send him a letter which he could have on record concerning
                    our commission to Persia.</p>
                <p>For the information of the Department I give you herewith carbon copy of the
                    letter I have written in response to this request.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">C. V. Vickrey</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d706-a1.xml" xpointer="d706-a1"/>
            </div>
